    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Tenure-Track%29%2C-Division-of-Industrial-Design/28092-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate  Professor (Tenure-Track), Division of Industrial Design",
      "description": "Associate  Professor (Tenure-Track), Division of Industrial Design Job Details | National University of Singapore Associate  Professor (Tenure-Track), Division of Industrial Design By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Associate  Professor (Tenure-Track), Division of Industrial Design University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Division of Industrial Design Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 10/03/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate  Professor (Tenure-Track), Division of Industrial Design University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Division of Industrial Design Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 10/03/2026 Job Description The Division of Industrial Design in the College of Design and Engineering is seeking highly qualified candidates who can join us as an Associate Professor and make significant contributions to the research and educational excellence of our programmes and university. We are looking for enthusiastic and motivated individuals with expertise in one or more of the following areas,  or other timely and relevant domains: •    Product, Service, and System innovation •    HCI and Emerging Technologies •    Healthcare, Social Innovation and Sustainability •    Design Theory, Processes, and Methods •    Practice-led Research •    Communication The successful candidate will receive a start-up research grant to undertake research of international excellence and contribute to knowledge exchange activities relative to their discipline. The successful candidate will engage in cross-disciplinary research and education programmes under the College of Design and Engineering. They will also make significant contributions to postgraduate programmes and PhD supervision. Qualifications Candidates are required to have a PhD in a design-related discipline. They should demonstrate exceptional research achievements or strong potential in their field, along with a proven ability to deliver impactful undergraduate and graduate education. A strong track record in research, teaching, or professional practice is essential, as is the capacity to drive the program’s growth and innovation. . Applications are to include: •    Detailed Curriculum Vitae (including research, teaching, professional practice, administrative experience) •    Publication and/or Project list •    Statement of Research citing up to five significant publications, creative work, or other scholarly contributions and explaining their significance (max. 3 pages) •    Statement of Teaching philosophy and methodology. Where available, evidence of teaching ability such as student achievements, feedback, or peer review reports (max. 3 pages) •    Design portfolio if applicable •    A list of referees (min. 6) with contact details (who will be contacted only with your concurrence) More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: College of Design and Engineering Department : Division of Industrial Design Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 28092 Req ID: 28092 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor/26635-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Job Details | National University of Singapore Assistant Professor By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Assistant Professor University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Division of Industrial Design Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 10/03/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Division of Industrial Design Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 10/03/2026 Job Description The Division of Industrial Design in the College of Design and Engineering is seeking highly qualified candidates who can join us as an Assistant Professor and make significant contributions to the research and educational excellence of our programmes and university. We are looking for enthusiastic and motivated individuals with expertise in one or more of the following areas,  or other timely and relevant domains: •    Product, Service, and System innovation •    HCI and Emerging Technologies •    Healthcare, Social Innovation and Sustainability •    Design Theory, Processes, and Methods •    Practice-led Research •    Communication The successful candidate will receive a start-up research grant to undertake research of international excellence and contribute to knowledge exchange activities relative to their discipline. The successful candidate will engage in cross-disciplinary research and education programmes under the College of Design and Engineering. They will also make significant contributions to postgraduate programmes and PhD supervision. Qualifications Candidates are required to have a PhD in a design related discipline, or one close to completion, with a strong track record in research, education, or professional engagements, and be able to advance the trajectory of the program. Applications are to include: •    Detailed Curriculum Vitae (including research, teaching, professional practice, administrative experience) •    Publication and/or Project list •    Statement of Research citing up to five significant publications, creative work, or other scholarly contributions and explaining their significance (max. 3 pages) •    Statement of Teaching philosophy and methodology. Where available, evidence of teaching ability such as student achievements, feedback, or peer review reports (max. 3 pages) •    Design portfolio if applicable •    A list of referees (min. 2) with contact details (who will be contacted only with your concurrence) More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: College of Design and Engineering Department : Division of Industrial Design Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 26635 Req ID: 26635 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
