    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Immunology-Translational-Research-Program-%28ITRP%29/32383-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) Job Details | National University of Singapore Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Microbiology And Immunology Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 10/04/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Microbiology And Immunology Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 10/04/2026 . Job Title: Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) Institution: National University of Singapore (NUS) Department/Faculty: Microbiology and Immunology, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Translational Research Program: Immunology Location: Singapore Appointment Type: Full-time, Tenure-track Position Summary The Immunology Translational Research Program (IDTRP) at the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for the position of tenure track Assistant Professor. We seek an exceptional and motivated individual to develop and lead a research program in Immunology, with a focus on translational research that bridges fundamental discoveries and clinical applications. The ideal candidate should have strong expertise and interests in neutrophil biology, particularly in the area of cellular ageing. The successful applicant will join a vibrant and collaborative team dedicated to advancing the understanding, prevention, and treatment of infectious diseases and cancer. . Key Responsibilities Establish an independent, externally funded research program in immunology with an emphasis on translational approaches. Conduct cutting-edge research that contributes to ITRP’s goals, including vaccine development, antimicrobial resistance, pathogen-host interactions, anti-tumor immunity, immune ageing, and public health interventions. Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams including clinicians, scientists, and other stakeholders to drive impactful research. Mentor and supervise undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral researchers. Teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in areas related to microbiology or immunology, anchored under the Department of Microbiology & Immunology. Publish high-quality, peer-reviewed research in leading journals and present findings at national and international conferences. Actively participate in ITRP’s events, workshops, and outreach activities. . Qualifications Essential: PhD, MD, or equivalent, with at least three years of postdoctoral experience in microbiology, immunology, epidemiology, or a related field. Proven track record of research excellence as evidenced by first author original high impact publications. Strong potential to secure competitive external funding. Expertise in translational research methodologies. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. Excellent communication and leadership skills. Desirable: Experience in teaching and curriculum development at the graduate level. Experience in mentoring and supervising research trainees. Research experience in neutrophil biology, microbial infection, and sepsis. Familiarity with regulatory and ethical requirements for translational research. . What We Offer Access to state-of-the-art research facilities and core resources. Opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers. Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package. A supportive environment fostering career development and advancement. Opportunities to engage in impactful, translational research that addresses pressing global health challenges. . Application Process Applicants should submit the following: A cover letter outlining their research and teaching interests. A detailed curriculum vitae (CV). A statement of research accomplishments and future plans. A statement of teaching philosophy. At least three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. . About Immunology Translational Research Program The Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) is driven by a vision to transform medicine through immunological research and a mission to advance collaborative, cutting-edge science that harnesses the immune system to improve human health. Grounded in the belief that a deep understanding of immune mechanisms is essential for preventing, diagnosing, and treating disease, ITRP fosters a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary environment where scientists and clinicians work together to generate impactful discoveries. Looking ahead, ITRP aims to establish itself as a leading centre for immunology in Southeast Asia by strengthening cross-institutional collaboration, partnering with hospitals to bring research from bench to bedside, and attracting and training the next generation of immunologists and clinician-scientists. Through these efforts, the programme strives to deliver meaningful advances that benefit patients and public health across the region. About Department of Microbiology and Immunology The Department of Microbiology and Immunology has distinguished itself in biomedical research and has a broad spectrum of expertise. Research in the Department encompasses very diverse questions and uses a wide variety of approaches, experimental systems, and techniques. Principal Investigators of the Department are internationally recognized for research on immunology, medical virology, bacteriology, parasitology, molecular biology and biotechnology. . About NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine The NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine is Singapore’s oldest and Asia’s top medical school, celebrating its 125th year anniversary in 2025. Today, the school produces cutting edge and impactful research, together with innovative education, seeking to impact change and enhance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The School is an integral part of a comprehensive university (NUS), with deep collaborative platforms across engineering, computer science, social science, public health, and others, and a long standing joint venture in the National University Health System (NUHS). The NUHS ecosystem is Singapore’s premier Academic Health Centre, encompassing three tertiary hospitals (National University Hospital, Ng Teng Fong Hospital and Alexander Hospital), three national specialist centres (National University Heart Centre, National University Cancer Institute and National University Centre for Oral Health), a primary care system and three health schools (medical school, dental school and school of public health), lending invaluable resource for clinical and translational research, not commonly found elsewhere. Together with other healthcare partners and research institutes in Singapore, the school is an important player in Singapore’s vibrant research and biotech ecosystem. Req ID: 32383 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-%28Epidemiology%29/26529-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor (Epidemiology)",
      "description": "Professor (Epidemiology) Job Details | National University of Singapore Professor (Epidemiology) By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Professor (Epidemiology) University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 03/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor (Epidemiology) University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 03/07/2026 Job Description The National University of Singapore – which is the top ranked university in Asia – is recruiting full-time Professors for the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health (SSHSPH). All positions are tenure-track appointment (i.e. appointees are given fixed contracts for up to 7 years, with the goal of obtaining tenured appointments at the end of this period). In additional to an attractive salary and benefits package, new faculty members are eligible for a start-up grant to initiate their independent stream of research and subsidised university accommodation, subject to prevailing terms and conditions. Researchers in the following areas are particularly encouraged to apply: Investigating the distribution and determinants of non-communicable and infectious diseases in populations and applying epidemiological methods to understand disease patterns and identify risk factors. Developing and applying mathematical models to predict disease trends and evaluate the potential impact of interventions, supporting the formulation of effective public health strategies and policies. Simulating disease transmission dynamics and intervention scenarios to assess the potential impacts of public health interventions, enhancing preparedness and response strategies for disease outbreaks. Engaging with SSHSPH’s large-scale cohort studies, such as the Singapore Chinese Health Study (SCHS) and the Singapore Multi-Ethnic Cohort (MEC) Study, to contribute to the development and utilisation of these cohort studies and to conduct translational epidemiological research that informs the development of effective public health interventions. Job Responsibilities R esearch respons i b ili t i es i nc l ude developing and establishing collaborative research proposals with NUS faculty for extramural funding. SSHSPH has several large-scale cohort studies including the Singapore Chinese Health Study and the Multi Ethnic Cohort Study. Applicants are expected to contribute to the development and use of these cohort studies and/or to conduct translational epidemiological research that informs the development of public health interventions. Teaching responsibilities include the development and teaching of courses in epidemiology and other areas of public health and the supervision of graduate students. Qualifications A recognised Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline with a strong post-doctoral professional and/or academic record; OR a qualified medical professional with postgraduate specialisation in occupational health, occupational medicine, or preventive medicine. Proven track record of publishing in high-impact international peer-reviewed journals. Experience in leading independent research studies or components within larger research programmes, and/or developing, leading, implementing and evaluating projects and programmes. Ability to generate and sustain an independent stream of research funding. Ability to teach public health courses at various levels (undergraduate, graduate and lifelong learners). Ability to work within multidisciplinary teams. Ability to work with and teach culturally diverse audiences. More Information To apply, please submit a cover letter specifying your research and/or teaching interests and experience, your curriculum vitae, names and contact details of 3 references. For more information on NUS please visit: www.nus.edu.sg . For more information about the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health please visit www.sph.nus.edu.sg . Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Req ID: 26529 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Cancer-Science-Institute%29/28463-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details | National University of Singapore Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 05/03/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 05/03/2026 Job Description The Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI) is seeking outstanding and visionary researchers for multiple faculty positions, ranging from Assistant to Full Professor . As a globally recognized leader with a reputation of excellence in cancer biology, immunology, and translational medicine, CSI is dedicated to transforming cancer detection, treatment, and prevention to improve patient outcomes. Our institute is purpose-built for cancer research and integrates cutting-edge technology, multidisciplinary approaches, and strong clinical collaborations to achieve groundbreaking discoveries. Our work spans the biological, computational, and engineering sciences, with a mission to address the unique cancer landscape of Asia while contributing to global progress. We are expanding our faculty to complement existing strengths and seed new, strategic directions in cancer research. We invite applications from exceptional scientists working in any area of cancer research, with particular interest in the following fields: Computational Biology of Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology Successful candidates will join a dynamic, collaborative environment and gain access to: State-of-the-art laboratories and world-class core facilities Generous start-up support and institutional research funding A competitive salary package aligned with global benchmarks Opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaborations within NUS and with global academic and industry partners Candidates should possess and demonstrate the following: A PhD and/or M.D. degree in a relevant discipline An established record of research excellence, with international competitiveness for their career stage A distinguished track record of research, publications, and leadership in cancer research Proven ability to secure funding and drive impactful, multidisciplinary research programs Application Documents To facilitate the application process, Candidates are invited to submit the following: Cover Letter Describe your background, expertise, and alignment with CSI's mission Comprehensive CV Include a full publication list, grants, awards, and leadership roles Key Achievements and Future Plans (up to 1500 words) Summarize your pivotal contributions to cancer research Outline your future research goals and potential synergies with CSI References Contact details of three senior colleagues willing to provide letters of reference Req ID: 28463 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Deputy-Director%2C-Centre-for-Infectious-Disease-Emergency-Response/33818-en_GB": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response",
      "description": "Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response Job Details | National University of Singapore Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 22/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 22/07/2026 Reporting to:    Programme Director, Professor Dale Fisher Job Purpose The Deputy Director provides strategic, scientific, and operational leadership for the Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response (CIDER), supporting the Director in advancing the Centre's mission to strengthen educational and operational efforts. The role oversees multidisciplinary programmes spanning outbreak preparedness, epidemiology, surveillance, health systems resilience, translational research, capacity building, and stakeholder engagement at national, regional, and global levels. The Deputy Director ensures the effective coordination of partnerships and emergency response initiatives, while fostering collaboration across NUS, government agencies, healthcare institutions, international organisations, and industry partners to enhance 's and the region's readiness for current and future infectious disease threats. Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Centre Development Support the Director in developing and implementing the Centre's strategic vision, goals, and operational plans Represent the Centre at institutional, national, regional, and international forums, committees, and working groups. Deputise for the Director as required and provide leadership during periods of increased Infectious Disease Emergency activity. Provide scientific oversight of the Centre's portfolio in infectious diseases, outbreak preparedness, pandemic response, surveillance, and health systems resilience. Develop and lead multidisciplinary initiatives involving faculty, clinicians, scientists, public health practitioners, and external collaborators. Facilitate the translation of research findings into policy, clinical practice, and emergency preparedness frameworks. Identify and secure grant funding from national and international funding agencies. Promote high-quality scientific publications, innovation, and knowledge dissemination. 2. Emergency Preparedness and Response Oversee the development of scenario planning exercises, simulations, and after-action reviews to strengthen preparedness capabilities. Maintain situational awareness of emerging global health threats and develop communication pathways to improve public and professional understanding Establish and implement mechanisms to assist development of the pillars of outbreak response regionally Develop an international network of trained outbreak responders 3. Partnerships and Stakeholder Engagement Build and maintain strategic partnerships with government agencies, healthcare institutions, academic centres, international organisations, NGOs, and industry. Facilitate collaborative projects that advance research, policy development, and emergency preparedness. Strengthen regional and global networks for infectious disease surveillance, capacity development, and rapid response. Serve as a key liaison between the Centre and external stakeholders. Promote the Centre's visibility, impact, and reputation through strategic engagement activities. . 4. Education, Training, and Capacity Building Oversee the development and delivery of educational programmes, professional training, workshops, and simulations related to infectious disease preparedness and response. Mentor faculty, administration, fellows, and students involved in Centre activities. Support workforce development initiatives aimed at strengthening public health and outbreak response capabilities. Foster interdisciplinary learning and collaboration across NUS faculties and external partners 5. Operations and Governance Oversee the effective management of Centre operations, resources, budgets, and personnel. Ensure compliance with NUS policies, funding requirements, governance standards, and regulatory obligations. Develop performance indicators and monitor programme outcomes and impact. Lead risk management, quality assurance, and continuous improvement initiatives. Support recruitment, performance management, and professional development of Centre staff 6. Policy and Knowledge Translation Provide expert advice on infectious disease preparedness, pandemic planning, and health security issues. Lead the preparation of policy briefs, technical reports, and strategic recommendations for stakeholders and decision-makers. Facilitate the translation of scientific evidence into actionable public health interventions. Contribute to national and international discussions on infectious disease preparedness, outbreak response, and health security. Requirements PhD, MD, MBBS with postgraduate qualifications, or equivalent doctorate in infectious diseases, epidemiology, public health, health policy, or a related field. Internationally recognised expertise in infectious diseases, outbreak response, epidemiology, public health preparedness, or health security. Senior leadership experience in academia, healthcare, government, public health agencies, or international organisations. Proven track record in research leadership, grant acquisition, and scholarly publications. Demonstrated experience in managing multidisciplinary teams and complex stakeholder environments. Strong strategic, communication, relationship-building, and organisational skills. Experience contributing to outbreak response. Demonstrably strong international multidisciplinary network Req ID: 33818 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Epidemiology%29/23560-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Epidemiology)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Epidemiology) Job Details | National University of Singapore Associate Professor (Epidemiology) By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Associate Professor (Epidemiology) University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 03/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor (Epidemiology) University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 03/07/2026 Associate Professor (Epidemiology) The National University of Singapore – which is the top ranked university in Asia – is recruiting full-time Associate Professors/Professors for the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health (SSHSPH). All positions are tenure-track appointment (i.e. appointees are given fixed contracts for up to 7 years, with the goal of obtaining tenured appointments at the end of this period). In additional to an attractive salary and benefits package, new faculty members are eligible for a start-up grant to initiate their independent stream of research and subsidised university accommodation, subject to prevailing terms and conditions. Researchers in the following areas are particularly encouraged to apply: Epidemiological research with a focus on molecular epidemiology, nutritional epidemiology, social epidemiology or behavioral epidemiology. Epidemiological research on obesity, type 2 diabetes, and cardiovascular diseases. Epidemiological research on cancer and non-communicable diseases. Qualifications Required qualifications are: an earned doctoral degree in a relevant discipline a strong track record of publications in international peer-reviewed journals ability to contribute to courses relevant to epidemiology and public health Responsibilities R esearch respons i b ili t i es i nc l ude developing and establishing collaborative research proposals with NUS faculty for extramural funding. SSHSPH has several large-scale cohort studies including the Singapore Chinese Health Study and the Multi Ethnic Cohort Study. Applicants are expected to contribute to the development and use of these cohort studies and/or to conduct translational epidemiological research that informs the development of public health interventions. Teaching responsibilities include the development and teaching of courses in epidemiology and other areas of public health and the supervision of graduate students. More Information To apply, please submit a cover letter specifying your research and/or teaching interests and experience, your curriculum vitae, names and contact details of 3 references. For more information on NUS, please visit: www.nus.edu.sg. For more information about the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, please visit www.sph.nus.edu.sg. Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Req ID: 23560 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Director-of-Advanced-Electron-Microscopy-Facility/33568-en_GB": {
      "title": "Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility",
      "description": "Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility Job Details | National University of Singapore Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility University-Level Unit: Office of the Deputy President(Res&Tech) Faculty/Department-Level Unit: S9 Advanced Microscopy Facility Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 01/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility University-Level Unit: Office of the Deputy President(Res&Tech) Faculty/Department-Level Unit: S9 Advanced Microscopy Facility Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 01/07/2026 Job Description NUS seeks to appoint a globally recognised scientific leader to serve as Director of the Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility, a flagship, university-level platform integrating state-of-the-art capabilities across materials science and life sciences. The Director will shape the facility into a globally leading centre for atomic-scale imaging and analysis, driving both frontier research and national-level capabilities. The Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility is a newly established university-level microscopy facility at NUS combining the state-of-the-art Electron and Scanning Tunnelling Microscopes for both the materials and life sciences. It is a centralised shared facility serving the research community at NUS, in Singapore, and beyond. It enables high-resolution 3D structure determination (CryoEM, FIB-SEM) and materials characterisation (such as AC-EM and STM). The facility aims to provide researchers with a unique competitive edge and students with excellent education and training opportunities. Driven by research of its members, it aims at being a world-leading research facility in Materials Science EM and Life Science cryoEM. Key Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership and direction to position the facility as a hub for large-scale international collaborations and flagship programmes. Set appropriate medium- and long-term research directions aligned with the facilities. Lead large, multi‑year research programmes by setting scientific directions and coordinating stakeholders. Set clear targets and user satisfaction measures. Develop the facility roadmap for future upgrades, new platforms, and capacity planning. Develop cost-recovery models (set internal/external rates), manage budgets and procurement. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety requirements and all NUS policies. Implement good data management practices. Qualifications NUS seeks to hire an outstanding research leader with strong relevant experience, possibly integrating material and life sciences EM. The appointment is anticipated at the Full Professor level and is expected to sustain an internationally leading research programme aligned with the facility’s strengths. Requirements Currently holding a faculty position with experience in life sciences, materials science and engineering, physics, or a related field. Evidence of significant core facility leadership. Proven track record of excellent publications and scientific contributions in the electron microscopy field. Distinguished records of research and administrative experience, and evidence of excellent leadership, interpersonal, and communication skills. Proven ability to lead teams, manage budgets, generate consistent external funding, run service operations, and deal with governments and corporate organisations locally and internationally. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 33568 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor%2C-Dept-of-Management-and-Organisation/33753-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation Job Details | National University of Singapore Assistant Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Assistant Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Management And Organisation Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 15/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Management And Organisation Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 15/07/2026 OPEN-RANK, TENURE-TRACK POSITIONS Position: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (tenure track) with a preference to hire a mid-career or senior candidate. Specialization: Human Resource Management / Organizational Behavior (broadly defined). We also welcome applicants trained in Industrial–Organizational Psychology, Social Psychology, Behavioral Economics, and related fields whose research speaks to HR/OB topics. The School and Environment Consistently ranked #1 in Asia, and AACSB / EQUIS accredited. Generous research support: competitive salary and benefits, start-up research grant,research assistants, behavioral labs, database subscriptions, and internal fundingschemes. Teaching load: 2 + 0 in the first two years for Assistant Professors; 3 + 0 thereafter. Subsidized, university-allocated housing (up to 9 years, subject to eligibility). Faculty publish regularly in AMJ, AMR, JAP, OBHDP, Org Science, PNAS, and othertop outlets. Singapore is a stable, safe, cosmopolitan city-state where English is an officiallanguage and the quality of life rivals that of major North American and European cities. Responsibilities Produce high-impact scholarly research. Teach in our Undergraduate, MSc, MBA, EMBA, PhD, and Executive Educationprograms. Supervise doctoral students and contribute to a vibrant research culture in a diverseand inclusive community. Required Qualifications A PhD in Management, OB, HRM, I/O Psychology, or a closely related discipline. A strong track record of publishing in top-tier journals. Commitment to excellent, innovative teaching. Application Procedure To ensure full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and brief statements of research and teaching interests to Jen Lee at mno-recruitment@nus.edu.sg, using the subject line “OB/HR Position,”. The search committee will be scheduling meeting times during the Academy of Management Annual Meeting. If you are interested in being considered for a meeting, please contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Hemant Kakkar, at hemant_kakkar@nus.edu.sg. Req ID: 33753 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
