      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation Job Details | National University of Singapore Professor / Associate Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Professor / Associate Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Management And Organisation Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 15/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor / Associate Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Management And Organisation Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 15/07/2026 OPEN-RANK, TENURE-TRACK POSITIONS Position: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (tenure track) with a preference to hire a mid-career or senior candidate. Specialization: Human Resource Management / Organizational Behavior (broadly defined). We also welcome applicants trained in Industrial–Organizational Psychology, Social Psychology, Behavioral Economics, and related fields whose research speaks to HR/OB topics. The School and Environment Consistently ranked #1 in Asia, and AACSB / EQUIS accredited. Generous research support: competitive salary and benefits, start-up research grant,research assistants, behavioral labs, database subscriptions, and internal fundingschemes. Teaching load: 2 + 0 in the first two years for Assistant Professors; 3 + 0 thereafter. Subsidized, university-allocated housing (up to 9 years, subject to eligibility). Faculty publish regularly in AMJ, AMR, JAP, OBHDP, Org Science, PNAS, and othertop outlets. Singapore is a stable, safe, cosmopolitan city-state where English is an officiallanguage and the quality of life rivals that of major North American and European cities. Responsibilities Produce high-impact scholarly research. Teach in our Undergraduate, MSc, MBA, EMBA, PhD, and Executive Educationprograms. Supervise doctoral students and contribute to a vibrant research culture in a diverseand inclusive community. Required Qualifications A PhD in Management, OB, HRM, I/O Psychology, or a closely related discipline. A strong track record of publishing in top-tier journals. Commitment to excellent, innovative teaching. Application Procedure To ensure full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and brief statements of research and teaching interests to Jen Lee at mno-recruitment@nus.edu.sg, using the subject line “OB/HR Position,”. The search committee will be scheduling meeting times during the Academy of Management Annual Meeting. If you are interested in being considered for a meeting, please contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Hemant Kakkar, at hemant_kakkar@nus.edu.sg. Req ID: 33745 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
