    "https://www.nus.edu.sg/careers/contact-us/": {
      "title": "Contact Us",
      "description": "Contact Us Privacy Notice This site uses cookies. By clicking accept or continuing to use this site, you agree to our use of cookies. For more details, please see our Privacy Policy . Accept Skip to content News Email Library Student Staff Home Why Join Us Compensation and Benefits Learning & Development Employee Engagement Living in Singapore About NUS Vision, Mission, Values Leadership Our Heritage Institutional Video Corporate Information News Job Opening Academic Positions Research & Other Teaching Positions​ Executive & Administrative Positions​ Management Associate Programme NUS Programmes NUS Presidential Young Professorship & Fellowship​ Data Literacy Programme – MSc ADS Scholarships Internships Contact Us Home Why Join Us Compensation and Benefits Learning & Development Employee Engagement Living in Singapore About NUS Vision, Mission, Values Leadership Our Heritage Institutional Video Corporate Information News Job Opening Academic Positions Research & Other Teaching Positions​ Executive & Administrative Positions​ Management Associate Programme NUS Programmes NUS Presidential Young Professorship & Fellowship​ Data Literacy Programme – MSc ADS Scholarships Internships Contact Us Contact Us National University of Singapore​ Office of Human Resources​ University Hall - Tan Chin Tuan Wing​ #UHT-04-01​ 21 Lower Kent Ridge Road​ Singapore 119077​ ​ For technical assistance relating to job application, please contact us here . National University of Singapore National University of Singapore​ 21 Lower Kent Ridge Road​ Singapore 119077​ +65 6516 6666 © National University of Singapore . All Rights Reserved. ​ Legal · Branding guidelines · Contact Us Scroll to Top"
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychology/32957-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Psychology Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Psychology Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor in Psychology University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Psychology Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 09/06/2026 National University of Singapore The Department of Psychology at the National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for two Assistant Professor positions. With regard to specialty, area is open, although preferences will be given to candidates with expertise in Clinical, Developmental and/or Quantitative Psychology. Candidates should hold a Ph.D. Candidates in Clinical Psychology should also have completed formal graduate-level training as a clinical psychologist. Consistently ranked as one of the top universities in Asia and the world, NUS is internationally respected for its high-quality teaching and research. Within NUS, the Department of Psychology has well-established undergraduate, graduate research and graduate clinical psychology professional training programmes. The department is made up of a diverse group of local and international faculty who are committed to excellence in teaching and research. Information on the department’s faculty, teaching and research programmes can be found at https://fass.nus.edu.sg/psy/ . NUS offers an internationally competitive 12-month salary package along with various benefits. There are also generous start-up packages tailored to the new faculty’s research needs. Beyond University resources, there are substantial opportunities to secure research grants from government agencies and other funding organizations. Interested applicants should submit their complete applications online at https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychology/32957-en_GB , comprising the following: CV Research statement: A statement (up to 3 pages) of major accomplishments in research, citing up to 5 significant publications, creative works or other scholarly contributions, and explaining their significance. Teaching statement: A statement (up to 3 pages) of teaching philosophy and methodology. List of all Ph.D. and postdoctoral supervisors or senior authors with close and regular collaborations (full name, institution and email address) Sample copies of significant publications (up to 5) Evidence of teaching ability (e.g. student feedback or peer review reports) and contributions to education (e.g. curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, production of teaching materials), if any Applicants should also arrange for at least 3 letters of reference (including one from the candidate’s main Ph.D. advisor, and one from the candidate’s postdoctoral supervisor) to be sent directly to Ms Loo Bee Bee at psylbb@nus.edu.sg . Review of applications begins 1 November 2026. We regret that only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Campus visits are expected to take place in January 2027. Prior to campus visits, remote pre-interviews with shortlisted candidates may be conducted. Queries may be directed to A/P Stuart Derbyshire, Chair of the Search Committee at stuart.derbyshire@nus.edu.sg . Req ID: 32957 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-%28Tenure-Track%29%2C-CSCB/32034-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor (Tenure Track), CSCB Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor (Tenure Track), CSCB Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant / Associate / Full Professor (Tenure Track), CSCB University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Research Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 10/03/2026 Job Description Duke-NUS Medical School (Duke-NUS), Singapore’s only graduate-entry medical school, is a landmark collaboration between two world-ranking institutions of higher education – Duke University and the National University of Singapore (NUS). Duke-NUS provides innovative education and impactful research to advance medicine and improve lives. Through our strategic partnership with Singapore Health Services (SingHealth), the largest public healthcare cluster in Singapore, the SingHealth/Duke-NUS Academic Medical Centre fosters cutting-edge collaborations in translational and clinical research, driving discoveries and solutions to global healthcare challenges. The Programme in Cancer & Stem Cell Biology (CSCB) is one of the Signature Research Programmes in Duke-NUS. The Programme is dedicated to advancing deep biological understanding of cancer and stem cell systems, spanning molecular, cellular, tissue, and organismal levels. We value research that challenges existing paradigms, uncovers new principles of disease biology, and lays the foundation for future translational and clinical advances. More information about CSCB faculty, research activities and facilities can be found at www.duke-nus.edu.sg/cscb . CSCB is seeking outstanding scientists who are driven by fundamental discoveries, interdisciplinary research, and intellectual curiosity, and who aspire to see their research ultimately inform better improved cancer prevention, diagnosis, and treatment, while advancing as well as driving the frontiers of novel drug development. The successful applicant should be highly collaborative and demonstrates strong enthusiasm to actively engage with both basic scientists and clinicians across disciplines. They will be expected to address complex research questions and compelling healthcare concerns, work within multidisciplinary teams to advance the frontiers of science, and contribute meaningfully to the School’s and the nation’s key priority areas. Job Requirements Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree with a strong background and proven track record across the full spectrum of cancer and stem cell biology. Areas of expertise may include, but are not limited to, RNA biology, therapeutics discovery, cancer immunology, functional genomics, computational and systems biology, cancer as an age-related disease, and emerging technologies. Excellence in any area of basic or discovery-driven cancer and stem cell research will be strongly considered. Research independence and demonstrated leadership in managing a productive research team. Exceptional track record in securing competitive research funding and publications in high impact scientific journals. Prior experience in translating research towards pre-clinical or commercial applications is desirable but not essential. Ability to mentor and train graduate students and postdoctoral research staff. Interested candidates should send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, and the names of three referees in support of their application via email at hr@duke-nus.edu.sg and attention it to: Administrative Chair Search Committee, CSCB Duke-NUS Medical School Applications will be open until the position is filled and we anticipate beginning interviewing candidates from June 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. More Information Location: Outram Campus Organization: Duke-NUS Medical School Department : Office of Research Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 32034 Req ID: 32034 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Biostatistics-and-Modelling%29%2C-Saw-Swee-Hock-School-of-Public-Health%2C-NUS/29949-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Biostatistics and Modelling), Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, NUS Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Biostatistics and Modelling), Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, NUS Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Biostatistics and Modelling), Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, NUS University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 25/06/2026 Job Description The National University of Singapore – which is the top ranked university in Asia – is recruiting full-time Assistant Professor(s) for the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health (SSHSPH) on the tenure track. For the tenure track, appointees are given fixed contracts for up to 7 years, with the goal of obtaining tenure at the end of this period. In addition to an attractive salary and benefits package, new faculty members may be eligible for a start-up grant to initiate their independent stream of research and subsidised university accommodation. The School is seeking to hire one or more biostatisticians, ideally those working on public health applications. The positions are specifically for faculty to work in the Biostatistics and Modelling Domain (BSMD) of SSHSPH. Researchers with existing research activities applying statistical methods in cancer, epidemiological studies, health promotion, physical activity, nutrition and primary care are particularly encouraged to apply. Qualifications Requirements: A recognized Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline with a strong post-doctoral research record; Track record of publishing in international peer-reviewed journals; Ability to generate and maintain an independent stream of funding; Ability to teach public health courses at both undergraduate and graduate levels; Ability to work in multidisciplinary teams; Ability to work with culturally diverse populations. Additional requirements to be appointed to the tenure track: Track record of publishing in high-impact international peer-reviewed journals; Experience in leading independent research studies; Ability to develop an internationally renowned research programme. Responsibilities Responsibilities include: establishing an independent research programme; providing statistical support for collaborative, multidisciplinary research; course design and teaching; and graduate student advising. To apply, please submit a cover letter specifying your research and teaching interests and experience, your curriculum vitae, and names and contacts of 3 references . For more information on NUS please visit: www.nus.edu.sg . For more information about the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health please visit www.sph.nus.edu.sg . Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Req ID: 29949 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Presidential-Young-Professor%29-in-Digital-Humanities/30354-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Digital Humanities Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Digital Humanities Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Digital Humanities University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Communications And New Media Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 04/06/2026 Job Description The Department of Communications and New Media at the National University of Singaporeapplications for tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) rank, with expertise in Digital Humanities in the field of Media Studies or Communication, specialized in one or more of the following areas: computational text or multimodal analysis, data visualisation and digital storytelling, digital archiving and preservation, network analysis and social media analytics, and human-computer interaction in humanities contexts . The National University of Singapore (NUS) is a leading research-intensive institution, consistently ranked among the world’s top universities. The University offers a competitive remuneration package, including medical, housing, relocation, and other benefits. Significant research start-up funding is also available Singapore is a modern, English-speaking city-state that serves as a global hub for commerce, finance, and transport. It offers a stable year-round climate and a cosmopolitan mix of cultures and languages. Qualifications PhD in digital humanities, visual communication, media studies, communication studies, information studies, cultural studies, or a closely related discipline. Application Instructions (Closing Deadline: 30 September 2026 @ 23:59hrs SGT) A Cover Letter : A cover letter explaining your interest in the position at NUS and the ambition of your research programme, together with a write-up on your top two papers, or the actual publications available. Curriculum Vitae (CV): A comprehensive CV including a complete list of all post-secondary educational qualifications with dates; employment history since the final degree with dates; complete list of publications and other creative output (separately listing books/monographs, refereed journal articles, and book chapters (distinguishing referred from non-refereed), and research in progress; honours and awards (if applicable): to include major keynote and plenary addresses, invited talks, elected membership in professional and learned societies, membership on editorial board of leading journals; teaching record; university service (if applicable); public and professional service (if applicable). Academic Certificates and Transcripts : Scanned copies of all relevant academic certificates and transcript. Teaching Statement : A statement of teaching philosophy and methodology (maximum 3 pages). Where available, please provide evidence of teaching ability such as student feedback or peer review reports, as well as evidence of other contributions to education (e.g., curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, production of teaching materials). Research Statement : A statement (maximum 3 pages) of major accomplishments in research, citing up to five significant publications, creative work or other scholarly contribution, and explaining their significance. Sample copies of these contributions should be provided (in the case of books, reviews should be provided). A research plan (3-page) with a proposed start-up research budget and utilisation plan for the next 3-5 years. External Reference Letters (For Assistant Professors): Candidate should arrange for at least three referees, including the PhD advisor, to send letters of reference directly to the department / faculty. The references need to include both the PhD advisor and Postdoctoral supervisor as applicable. Referees should benchmark your research performance against peers at equivalent and top institutions or programmes and must send their letters directly to cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For any questions, please email cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg . More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: Arts & Social Sciences Department : Communications And New Media Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 30354 Req ID: 30354 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Presidential-Young-Professor%29-in-Strategic-Communication/30228-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Strategic Communication Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Strategic Communication Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Strategic Communication University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Communications And New Media Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 04/06/2026 Job Description The Department of Communications and New Media at the National University of Singaporeapplications for tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) rank, with expertise in Strategic Communication in the field/s of PR/corporate communication, risk and crisis communication, organisational communication, advertising & marketing communications, public diplomacy, digital/social media for strategic communication . Candidates with previous industry experience in public relations and marketing communications are strongly encouraged to apply. The National University of Singapore (NUS) is a leading research-intensive institution, consistently ranked among the world’s top universities. The University offers a competitive remuneration package, including medical, housing, relocation, and other benefits. Significant research start-up funding is also available. Singapore is a modern, English-speaking city-state that serves as a global hub for commerce, finance, and transport. It offers a stable year-round climate and a cosmopolitan mix of cultures and languages. Qualifications PhD in Communication or closely related disciplines, with a specialisation in studying new media in social, corporate and governmental contexts with contemporary data and media methods. Candidates will also have evidence of excellence in both research and teaching, and demonstrate leadership in their fields commensurate with rank. Application Instructions (Closing Deadline: 30 September 2026 @ 23:59hrs SGT) A Cover Letter : A cover letter explaining your interest in the position at NUS and the ambition of your research programme, together with a write-up on your top two papers, or the actual publications available. Curriculum Vitae (CV) : A comprehensive CV including a complete list of all post-secondary educational qualifications with dates; employment history since the final degree with dates; complete list of publications and other creative output (separately listing books/monographs, refereed journal articles, and book chapters (distinguishing referred from non-refereed), and research in progress; honours and awards (if applicable): to include major keynote and plenary addresses, invited talks, elected membership in professional and learned societies, membership on editorial board of leading journals; teaching record; university service (if applicable); public and professional service (if applicable). Academic Certificates and Transcripts : Scanned copies of all relevant academic certificates and transcript. Teaching Statement : A statement of teaching philosophy and methodology (maximum 3 pages). Where available, please provide evidence of teaching ability such as student feedback or peer review reports, as well as evidence of other contributions to education (e.g., curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, production of teaching materials). Research Statement: A statement (maximum 3 pages) of major accomplishments in research, citing up to five significant publications, creative work or other scholarly contribution, and explaining their significance. Sample copies of these contributions should be provided (in the case of books, reviews should be provided). A research plan (3-page) with a proposed start-up research budget and utilisation plan for the next 3-5 years. External Reference Letters: Candidate should arrange for at least three referees, including the PhD advisor, to send letters of reference directly to the department / faculty. The references need to include both the PhD advisor and Postdoctoral supervisor as applicable. Referees should benchmark your research performance against peers at equivalent and top institutions or programmes and must send their letters directly to cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For any questions, please email cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg . More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: Arts & Social Sciences Department : Communications And New Media Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 30228 Req ID: 30228 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-%28HSRPH-MO%29/31872-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor (HSRPH/ MO) Job Details",
      "description": "Professor (HSRPH/ MO) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor (HSRPH/ MO) University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Research Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 27/08/2026 Job Description The Signature Research Programme in Health Services Research and Population Health (“HSRPH”) in Duke-NUS Medical School is a centre of academic excellence for research and education on Population Health and the organisation, funding and delivery of health services. The programme’s focus is on population health and clinical service innovation in an increasingly complex and connected world. The major research focus of HSRPH is the organisation and delivery of health and social services in the context of an ageing population. We are also developing a range of education activities for healthcare professionals including short courses, graduate certificates, Master’s courses and PhD programmes. We invite applications for a tenure-track/tenured faculty position based in Singapore at the rank of Associate Professor/ Professor. Job title, salaries and benefits will be commensurate with the candidate’s accomplishments and experiences. Job Responsibilities: We are seeking a researcher whose research methods might include quantitative and qualitative research, behavioural, decision and implementation science. Focus areas might include mental health, ageing, environment and health, population health, healthcare finance and health policy  with the aim to inform clinical and public policy decision making; and is able to lead and publish research that moves the discipline forward. The ideal candidate will enjoy a multidisciplinary environment and will establish an innovative, pragmatic, world leading research agenda. He/She will provide consultancy services, build capacity by mentoring clinicians and other researchers and supporting relevant education activities. Opportunities exist for productive collaborations with world-class researchers within HSRPH and with SingHealth clinicians and other staff and other national health care organizations, as well as the SingHealth Duke-NUS Global Health Institute. This tenure-track/tenured position represents an outstanding opportunity for an established investigator. Qualifications Requirements & Responsibilities: •    Bring together and develop a team of researchers. •    Create a distinctive research programme. •    Track record of applied research and methods-based publications. •    Track record of independent research and collaboration with clinical and policy partners. •    Track record in securing research grants. Other Skills and Personal Attributes Required: •    A relevant PhD or equivalent qualification •    Leadership skills •    An ability to work collaboratively. •    Existing mentoring skills or willingness to develop these •    Ability to work with applied projects and methodology •    Skills in communicating complex ideas to non-technical audiences We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 31872 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Presidential-Young-Professor%29-in-Computational-Communication/30232-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Computational Communication",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Computational Communication Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Computational Communication University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Communications And New Media Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 04/06/2026 Job Description Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) in Computational Communication The Department of Communications and New Media at the National University of Singapore invites applications for tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor (Presidential Young Professor) rank, with expertise in one or more of the following areas: media studies, visual communication, science communication, cultural studies, and computational communication . We are especially interested in candidates with a focus on Asia-centred and artificial intelligence research. The NUS Presidential Young Professorship and NUS Presidential Fellowship Awards aim to attract, support, and empower the brightest and most promising young academics at the early stages of their careers, helping them develop into world-class scholars. As an academic at NUS, you will have the opportunity to work alongside a diverse and dynamic community of scholars and students, pursue excellence and innovation, and make a positive societal impact. Successful PYP candidates are awarded a start-up grant package of either SGD 250,000 or SGD 750,000, depending on the demands of their research programme. They are also granted an additional SGD 250,000 for discretionary spending. The National University of Singapore (NUS) is a leading research-intensive university that is consistently ranked among the world’s top universities. Remuneration is competitive and includes medical, housing, relocation and other benefits. Significant research start-up funding is available. Singapore is a modern, English-speaking city state that is connected to the world via global commerce, finance and transport networks with a stable climate year round and a cosmopolitan mix of cultures and languages. Qualifications PhD in Communication or closely related discipline by date of appointment, with a specialisation in methods for digital data collection, analytics, and/or visualisation. Evidence of excellence in computational communication research and teaching. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to conduct research that applies data science in communication contexts such as data journalism and data-driven strategic communication for health, marketing, or politics, and considers the implications of data-driven methods for building and validating communication and/or information theory. Candidates must have experience with computational techniques using R or Python and the ability to teach courses in computational communication, social media research, network analysis, and/or time series analysis. Application Instructions (Closing Deadline: 30 September 2026 @ 23:59hrs SGT) A Cover Letter : A cover letter explaining your interest in the position at NUS and the ambition of your research programme, together with a write-up on your top two papers, or the actual publications available. Curriculum Vitae (CV): A comprehensive CV including a complete list of all post-secondary educational qualifications with dates; employment history since the final degree with dates; complete list of publications and other creative output (separately listing books/monographs, refereed journal articles, and book chapters (distinguishing referred from non-refereed), and research in progress; honours and awards (if applicable): to include major keynote and plenary addresses, invited talks, elected membership in professional and learned societies, membership on editorial board of leading journals; teaching record; university service (if applicable); public and professional service (if applicable). Academic Certificates and Transcripts : Scanned copies of all relevant academic certificates and transcript. Teaching Statement : A statement of teaching philosophy and methodology (maximum 3 pages). Where available, please provide evidence of teaching ability such as student feedback or peer review reports, as well as evidence of other contributions to education (e.g., curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, production of teaching materials). Research Statement : A statement (maximum 3 pages) of major accomplishments in research, citing up to five significant publications, creative work or other scholarly contribution, and explaining their significance. Sample copies of these contributions should be provided (in the case of books, reviews should be provided). A research plan (3-page) with a proposed start-up research budget and utilisation plan for the next 3-5 years. External Reference Letters (For Assistant Professors): Candidate should arrange for at least three referees, including the PhD advisor, to send letters of reference directly to the department / faculty. The references need to include both the PhD advisor and Postdoctoral supervisor as applicable. Referees should benchmark your research performance against peers at equivalent and top institutions or programmes and must send their letters directly to cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg . External Review Letters (For Associate Professors & Professors) : Provide a minimum list of six recommended external reviewers, including their names, contact details, and your relationship to each. These external reviewers should preferably not be close collaborators, nor your PhD or postdoctoral supervisors. A one-page biography of each external reviewer must be included. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For any questions, please email cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg . More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: Arts & Social Sciences Department : Communications And New Media Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 30232 Req ID: 30232 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28ECE%29/33029-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (ECE) Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (ECE) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (ECE) University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Electrical and Computer Engineering Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 22/05/2026 Job Description The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) is seeking a candidate at the rank of Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in the area of machine learning and artificial intelligence. The candidate is expected lead active and externally funded research program and collaborative research with colleagues in other disciplines to address challenges that achieve scientific and societal impact are encouraged. Besides research, the candidate is also expected to contribute actively to teaching and service roles at the Department, College, or University level. Interested applicants are invited to submit a detailed CV, a teaching philosophy statement, list of publications, statement of research interests and plans, contact details of at least 3 referees, and the NUS Personal Data Consent for Job Applicants. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a campus visit and interview. Applications will be accepted until the available position is filled. Qualifications The successful candidate must have an earned doctorate in Electrical Engineering and/or Computer Engineering or an allied field. Candidates must have an established track record in research. Req ID: 33029 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor%2C-Strategy-and-Policy/33362-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details",
      "description": "Associate Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor, Strategy and Policy University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Strategy And Policy Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 16/06/2026 Job Overview The Department of Strategy and Policy at NUS Business School invites applications from Strategy / Management of Technology / Entrepreneurship scholars for tenure-track and tenured positions (all ranks). Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or be near completion. Selection for full / associate ranks will be based on an established publication record and proven teaching experience. Selection for the assistant rank will be based on potential for publications in top journals and effective teaching. About NUS The National University of Singapore (NUS) is Singapore’s flagship university, which offers a global approach to education, research and entrepreneurship, with a focus on Asian perspectives and expertise. We have 16 colleges, faculties and schools with more than 40,000 students from 100 countries enriching our vibrant and diverse community. We have also established our NUS Overseas Colleges programme in more than 15 cities around the world. For more information on NUS, please visit www.nus.edu.sg . About NUS Business School The National University of Singapore (NUS) Business School is known for providing management thought leadership from an Asian perspective, enabling its students and corporate partners to leverage global knowledge and Asian insights. The school has consistently received top rankings in the Asia-Pacific region by independent publications and agencies, such as The Financial Times, Economist Intelligence Unit, and QS Top MBA, in recognition of the quality of its programmes, faculty research and graduates. The Department of Strategy and Policy ( https://bschool.nus.edu.sg/strategy-policy/) numbers about 30 faculty members representing more than 13 nationalities, who regularly publish in major international journals including the Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Administrative Science Quarterly, Management Science, and Organization Science . For more information, please visit bschool.nus.edu.sg. Application Procedures We offer a conducive research environment with generous research funding, as well as competitive remuneration and benefits. Prospective applicants should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter outlining their research interests and teaching experience; (2) curriculum vitae (CV); (3) samples of research papers or a job market paper; and (4) three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates). For junior applicants, all application materials should be submitted via email to bprecruit@nus.edu.sg no later than September 1, 2026 , to receive full consideration. Mid-career applicants have no fixed deadline and are encouraged to apply at their earliest convenience. Preliminary interviews will be conducted at the Academy of Management (AOM) Annual Meeting in Philadelphia. While participation in these interviews is not mandatory, applicants who wish to be considered for an AOM interview should submit their CV by July 10, 2026 . Commitment to Fair and Inclusive Employment We believe in creating a workplace that values diversity, promotes equal opportunities, and fosters an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, and select faculty solely based on merit and job-related criteria, such as skills, experience, and ability to perform the job. We do not discriminate on the basis of age, ethnicity, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability, and are committed to ensuring a fair and equitable recruitment process for all. We continue to uphold these principles and strive to create a workplace that is welcoming, respectful, and supportive for all. Req ID: 33362 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/DEAN%2C-YONG-LOO-LIN-SCHOOL-OF-MEDICINE%2C-NATIONAL-UNIVERSITY-OF-SINGAPORE/33786-en_GB": {
      "title": "DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE Job Details",
      "description": "DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE Job Details | National University of Singapore DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Others Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 20/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Others Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 20/07/2026 Background The National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for the post of Dean, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine. Founded in 1905, the NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine is Singapore’s first and largest medical school, celebrating its 120th year anniversary in 2025. It ranked 13th in the Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026 for Medical and Health and 17th in the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings by Subject 2026 for Medicine. Today, the school conducts cutting edge research and delivers innovative education, generating high impact solutions that advance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The School is an integral part of NUS, a comprehensive university with deep interdisciplinary collaborations across engineering, computer science, social science, public health, and other fields. It also benefits from a long-standing partnership  within the National University Health System (NUHS), creating a unique environment that seamlessly combines education, research and patient care. The NUHS ecosystem brings together three tertiary hospitals (National University Hospital, Ng Teng Fong Hospital and Alexandra Hospital), three national specialist centres (National University Heart Centre, National University Cancer Institute and National University Centre for Oral Health), a comprehensive primary care system and three NUS schools in Medicine, Dentistry and Public Health. Together with other healthcare partners and research institutes in Singapore, the school is a key contributor to Singapore’s vibrant biomedical ecosystem. For more information, please visit the website: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine . Profile of Candidate As the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine advances its global leadership in medical education, biomedical research, and healthcare innovation, NUS seeks a visionary and people-centred leader who can articulate a compelling strategic direction for the School; foster an inclusive, collaborative, and high-performing academic culture; strengthen partnerships across the University, healthcare system, and international community; attract, develop, and retain outstanding and diverse faculty, students, and staff; and lead the School in addressing emerging opportunities in healthcare, technology, and medical education. The Dean must be able to inspire trust, exercise integrity and sound judgement, unite the School around a shared vision, and possess an exemplary scholarly record and international reputation suitable for appointment as a tenured Full Professor in the School. NUS is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion in its community. We encourage applications by individuals who embody and embrace these values. Submission The Search Committee welcomes applications and nominations of suitable candidates. Application materials should include a full Curriculum Vitae and a broad vision statement for the School. Applications, enquiries or nominations should be sent by 31 October 2026 to: Professor HO Ghim Wei Vice-Provost (Academic Affairs) Chair, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Dean Search Committee National University of Singapore c/o Ms Dolly Teo YLLSOM Dean Search Committee Secretariat E-mail: dollyteo@nus.edu.sg All nominations and applications will be kept in the strictest confidence. We appreciate your kind understanding that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 33786 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor%2C-Strategy-and-Policy/33363-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details",
      "description": "Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor, Strategy and Policy University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Strategy And Policy Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 16/06/2026 Job Overview The Department of Strategy and Policy at NUS Business School invites applications from Strategy / Management of Technology / Entrepreneurship scholars for tenure-track and tenured positions (all ranks). Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or be near completion. Selection for full / associate ranks will be based on an established publication record and proven teaching experience. Selection for the assistant rank will be based on potential for publications in top journals and effective teaching. About NUS The National University of Singapore (NUS) is Singapore’s flagship university, which offers a global approach to education, research and entrepreneurship, with a focus on Asian perspectives and expertise. We have 16 colleges, faculties and schools with more than 40,000 students from 100 countries enriching our vibrant and diverse community. We have also established our NUS Overseas Colleges programme in more than 15 cities around the world. For more information on NUS, please visit www.nus.edu.sg . About NUS Business School The National University of Singapore (NUS) Business School is known for providing management thought leadership from an Asian perspective, enabling its students and corporate partners to leverage global knowledge and Asian insights. The school has consistently received top rankings in the Asia-Pacific region by independent publications and agencies, such as The Financial Times, Economist Intelligence Unit, and QS Top MBA, in recognition of the quality of its programmes, faculty research and graduates. The Department of Strategy and Policy ( https://bschool.nus.edu.sg/strategy-policy/) numbers about 30 faculty members representing more than 13 nationalities, who regularly publish in major international journals including the Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Administrative Science Quarterly, Management Science, and Organization Science . For more information, please visit bschool.nus.edu.sg. Application Procedures We offer a conducive research environment with generous research funding, as well as competitive remuneration and benefits. Prospective applicants should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter outlining their research interests and teaching experience; (2) curriculum vitae (CV); (3) samples of research papers or a job market paper; and (4) three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates). For junior applicants, all application materials should be submitted via email to bprecruit@nus.edu.sg no later than September 1, 2026 , to receive full consideration. Mid-career applicants have no fixed deadline and are encouraged to apply at their earliest convenience. Preliminary interviews will be conducted at the Academy of Management (AOM) Annual Meeting in Philadelphia. While participation in these interviews is not mandatory, applicants who wish to be considered for an AOM interview should submit their CV by July 10, 2026 . Commitment to Fair and Inclusive Employment We believe in creating a workplace that values diversity, promotes equal opportunities, and fosters an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, and select faculty solely based on merit and job-related criteria, such as skills, experience, and ability to perform the job. We do not discriminate on the basis of age, ethnicity, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability, and are committed to ensuring a fair and equitable recruitment process for all. We continue to uphold these principles and strive to create a workplace that is welcoming, respectful, and supportive for all. Req ID: 33363 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-%28Cancer-Science-Institute%29/28465-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details",
      "description": "Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 01/07/2026 Job Description The Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI) is seeking outstanding and visionary researchers for multiple faculty positions, ranging from Assistant to Full Professor . As a globally recognized leader with a reputation of excellence in cancer biology, immunology, and translational medicine, CSI is dedicated to transforming cancer detection, treatment, and prevention to improve patient outcomes. Our institute is purpose-built for cancer research and integrates cutting-edge technology, multidisciplinary approaches, and strong clinical collaborations to achieve groundbreaking discoveries. Our work spans the biological, computational, and engineering sciences, with a mission to address the unique cancer landscape of Asia while contributing to global progress. We are expanding our faculty to complement existing strengths and seed new, strategic directions in cancer research. We invite applications from exceptional scientists working in any area of cancer research, with particular interest in the following fields: Computational Biology of Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology Successful candidates will join a dynamic, collaborative environment and gain access to: State-of-the-art laboratories and world-class core facilities Generous start-up support and institutional research funding A competitive salary package aligned with global benchmarks Opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaborations within NUS and with global academic and industry partners Candidates should possess and demonstrate the following: A PhD and/or M.D. degree in a relevant discipline An established record of research excellence, with international competitiveness for their career stage A distinguished track record of research, publications, and leadership in cancer research Proven ability to secure funding and drive impactful, multidisciplinary research programs Application Documents To facilitate the application process, Candidates are invited to submit the following: Cover Letter Describe your background, expertise, and alignment with CSI's mission Comprehensive CV Include a full publication list, grants, awards, and leadership roles Key Achievements and Future Plans (up to 1500 words) Summarize your pivotal contributions to cancer research Outline your future research goals and potential synergies with CSI References Contact details of three senior colleagues willing to provide letters of reference Req ID: 28465 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Cancer-Science-Institute%29/28471-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 01/07/2026 Job Description The Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty positions at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level. CSI is a globally recognized research institute committed to advancing the frontiers of cancer biology, immunology, and translational medicine . With a mission to transform cancer detection, treatment, and prevention, our purpose-built institute leverages state-of-the-art infrastructure, multidisciplinary expertise, and strong clinical partnerships to deliver impactful, patient-centered research. Our scientific community spans biological, computational, and engineering disciplines, focusing on the unique cancer challenges of Asia while contributing meaningfully to global cancer research. We are seeking exceptional, visionary scientists to join our expanding faculty and shape new research directions that complement our existing strengths. Candidates from all areas of cancer research are welcome, with particular interest in the following domains: Computational Biology of Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology We welcome applications from scientists who meet the following criteria: A Ph.D. and/or M.D. in a relevant field A strong track record of research excellence, commensurate with career stage A distinguished portfolio of publications, research leadership, and scientific contributions in cancer research Demonstrated success in securing competitive research funding and leading multidisciplinary research initiatives Successful candidates will join a vibrant and collaborative research environment with access to: World-class laboratory facilities and advanced core technologies Competitive start-up packages and institutional research funding A globally benchmarked salary and benefits package Extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations across NUS and with international academic and industry partners Application Documents To apply, please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Describe your background, research interests, and how your work aligns with CSI’s mission and strategic priorities. Comprehensive Curriculum Vitae Include a complete list of publications, grants awarded, honors, and leadership roles. Statement of Key Achievements and Future Research Plans (up to 1500 words) Highlight your most significant contributions to cancer research. Articulate your future research vision and potential synergies with CSI. Three References Provide contact details of three senior scientists who can speak to your qualifications and research impact. Req ID: 28471 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
