 Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology Successful candidates will join a dynamic, collaborative environment and gain access to: State-of-the-art laboratories and world-class core facilities Generous start-up support and institutional research funding A competitive salary package aligned with global benchmarks Opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaborations within NUS and with global academic and industry partners Candidates should possess and demonstrate the following: A PhD and/or M.D. degree in a relevant discipline An established record of research excellence, with international competitiveness for their career stage A distinguished track record of research, publications, and leadership in cancer research Proven ability to secure funding and drive impactful, multidisciplinary research programs Application Documents To facilitate the application process, Candidates are invited to submit the following: Cover Letter Describe your background, expertise, and alignment with CSI's mission Comprehensive CV Include a full publication list, grants, awards, and leadership roles Key Achievements and Future Plans (up to 1500 words) Summarize your pivotal contributions to cancer research Outline your future research goals and potential synergies with CSI References Contact details of three senior colleagues willing to provide letters of reference Req ID: 30188 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
